  "query_preview": "..\n(Saturday through Wednesday)\nIssued at 1159 AM MST Thu Nov 5 2026\n\nAfter the shortwave passes, pleasant weather is likely throughout \nthe long term period and potentially stretching even further. \nPressure heights will gradually rise throughout next week, bringing \na slow but gradual rise in temperatures each day. Winds are looking \nto be primarily light with only a few breezes across the state. The \nexception to this looks to be Wednesday as a trough digs over the \nupper Great Plains. This is currently forecast to drop a cold front \ndown the Front Range and into eastern NM, however there is only \nmoderate confidence with this at the moment given some sharp \ndisagreement between deterministic models on timing. A return to \nsome unsettled weather may be in store for next weekend, but \nsignificant model and ensemble spread exists for how a system \naffecting the Pacific Coast moves inland.",
